**Analysis of Search Results for Audi A4 Cabriolet TFSI (B7):**

*   **Generations:** The A4 Cabriolet was B6 (2002-2005) and B7 (2005-2009) (Source 2, 8, 11, 26). The 2.0 TFSI engine was introduced in the B7 (Source 1, 7, 8, 19, 26). I will focus on the B7 A4 Cabriolet 2.0 TFSI (2005-2009).
*   **Engine:** 2.0 TFSI (Turbo Fuel Stratified Injection) Inline 4, 1984 cm³ (121.1 cu-in), 197-200 HP, 206-207 lb-ft torque (Source 1, 7, 8, 19).
*   **Performance (2.0 TFSI 200 HP):** 0-60 mph in 7.5-7.9 seconds (Source 7, 9). Top speed 148 mph / 238 km/h (Source 1, 7, 10).
*   **Drive Type:** FWD and Quattro AWD were available (Source 7, 19).
*   **Transmission:** Manual (6-speed), Multitronic CVT (FWD), and Tiptronic Automatic (Quattro) were available (Source 7, 10, 12, 26). Tiptronic is a conventional automatic. Multitronic CVT has known issues (Source 32).
*   **Fuel Economy (2.0 TFSI):** Combined 34.0 mpg UK (Source 9, 12, 26). Urban 24.4 mpg, Extra Urban 42.2 mpg (Source 9).
*   **CO2 Emissions (2.0 TFSI):** 199 g/km (Source 1). Honest John lists 176 g/km for 2.0 TDI, 2.0T FSI is listed at 34.0 mpg which corresponds to higher CO2 than the TDI. Let's use 199 g/km.
*   **Dimensions:** Length ~4570-4573mm, Width ~1777-1780mm, Height ~1390-1391mm, Wheelbase ~2650-2654mm (Source 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 26).
*   **Cargo Space:** 246 L (8.69 cu ft) with top down, 315 L (11.12 cu ft) with top up (Source 1, 2, 4, 7, 26). This is small.
*   **Rear Space:** Limited rear legroom (Source 11, 13).
*   **Ground Clearance:** ~10.9 cm / ~4.3 inches (Source 5, 6). This is low.
*   **Turn Radius:** ~11.1m / ~36.4 ft (Source 4, 7). This is average.
*   **Seats:** 4 (Source 2, 4).
*   **Reliability/Repair Risk:** 2.0 TFSI (EA113 engine) had some known issues like oil consumption, PCV valve, and cam follower wear, especially with long-life service intervals (Source 15, 28). Overall Audi reliability is often considered average to slightly below average for premium brands (Source 23). RepairPal gives the A4 (2007) a 3.5/5 reliability rating, average ownership costs, and average frequency/severity of repairs (Source 33). There's a 27.69% chance of a major repair in the first 10 years (Source 23). Convertible roof mechanism can have issues like rear glass separating or the trunk 'roof-box' breaking (Source 34).
*   **Maintenance Cost:** Audi maintenance is generally higher than average (Source 23). RepairPal estimates $589 annual maintenance cost for a 2007 A4 (Source 33). CarEdge estimates $9,649 over 10 years, slightly better than the luxury sedan average (Source 23).
*   **Insurance Group:** 2.0 TFSI is Group 34E (UK) (Source 9, 12). This is above average.
*   **Price (Used):** Used prices in the UK range from ~£2,500 to ~£5,000+ depending on condition, mileage, year, and spec (Source 9, 14, 22, 30, 36, 37). This is well below the new car average.
*   **Total Cost of Ownership:** Likely average to slightly above average for an older premium car due to potential maintenance/repair costs balancing low purchase price.
*   **Interior/Features:** Dated MMI, small screen (optional Nav Plus), optional Bose audio, optional heated seats, dual-zone climate control standard, power seats, cruise control, basic ADAS (ABS, ESP, airbags, roll-over protection) (Source 13, 19, 21, 22, 24, 26). Optional acoustic roof improved cabin noise (Source 11). Steering feel improved in B7 but still criticized as light/lacking feel (Source 11, 13, 27). Ride comfort improved in B7 (Source 11, 19).
*   **ADAS:** Basic for modern standards (Source 13, 18, 24, 38).
*   **Visibility:** Convertible design impacts rear visibility (common issue) -> -0.50.
*   **Headlights:** Optional Bi-Xenon (Source 11). Average compared to modern LEDs.
*   **Security:** Standard for its time (alarm, immobilizer) -> 0.00.
*   **Infotainment:** Dated system, small screen, limited connectivity (optional Bluetooth, no modern smartphone integration) (Source 18, 21, 24). Aftermarket Android units are available (Source 24, 29).
*   **Comfort/Convenience:** Dual-zone climate, power seats, optional heated seats, auto lights/wipers (optional), parking sensors (optional) (Source 13, 21, 22). Average for its time, below modern average.
*   **Style:** Single-frame grille, sleek profile (Source 11, 13, 21). Modernity is dated. Aggression is mild.
*   **Brand/Model/Trim Prestige:** Audi is premium (0.50). A4 is a core model (0.00). TFSI is an engine variant, not a specific trim prestige level like S line or Sport. Standard trim is average (0.00).
*   **Interior Luxury/Tech:** Quality materials for its time, but tech is dated (Source 11, 13, 21, 27).

